<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57095" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κηλ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>charm, bewitch, beguile</i>, esp. by music, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόρην ὕμνοισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					359
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾠδαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ly.</u>
					206b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κηλῶν τῇ φωνῇ ὥσπερ Ὀρφεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					315a
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Ind.</u>
				12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὕτως ἐκήλει</span>, of
			Pericles as an orator, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				94.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπᾴδων κ.</span>
			<i>charm</i> by incantation, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				267d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ με κηλήσεις τρόπῳ</span>;
				<i><span class="en">
				Achae.
				17.2
			</span></i>; of bribery, <i><span class="en">
				Theopomp.Com.
				30
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κηλεῖται ἀοιδαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archil.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.20
			</span></i> K., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>Dith.</u>
				2.22
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ σοῦ ὥσπερ ὄφις κηληθῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					358b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ δώρων κηλούμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					885d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφ᾽ ἡδονῆς κηληθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					413c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφ᾽ οἷς κατορθώσαντες εὐφρανθήσονται,
					τούτοις κεκήληνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					1.191
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρὰ ταῖς Σειρῆσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EE</u>
					1230b35
				</span></i>
			: rarely in good sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδείᾳ τὸν νοῦν κηληθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					333c
				</span></i>
			.</div>
